#: ../../source/api/PyFlow.command_control_extension_tcp.rst:2
#: a6084f2941f34f579f28c55e9dfb768d
msgid "PyFlow.command\\_control\\_extension\\_tcp module"
msgstr "PyFlow.command\\_control\\_extension\\_tcp模块"

#: 9209095513ec402980427a0ddd988219 PyFlow.command_control_extension_tcp:1 of
#, fuzzy
msgid "Command-control extension for the TCP protocol."
msgstr "PyFlow.command\\_control\\_extension\\_tcp模块"

#: 47d5c98c564241a6911eff0abea987ec PyFlow.command_control_extension_tcp:3 of
msgid ""
"One command batch, run by every listed client, with each client's output "
"collected on the server:"
msgstr ""

#: PyFlow.command_control_extension_tcp:6 b14c7eec72b44dc1bd343997acf1cf44 of
msgid "/command <command_1> ... <command_n> <client_1> ... <client_m>"
msgstr ""

#: PyFlow.command_control_extension_tcp:7 fe2fb5a737534088b175ea340c1763f9 of
msgid ""
"typed on the server console. Every client runs the whole command list in "
"a single shell session, in order, so state such as a changed working "
"directory carries over from one command to the next: ``/command \"cd "
"/path/to/search\" \"ls ./\" \"(ip, port)\"`` lists the files of "
"``/path/to/search``, while sending ``cd`` and ``ls`` as two separate "
"``/command`` lines does not."
msgstr ""

#: 29a70dd76bf34e90a9ea54ac27202289 PyFlow.command_control_extension_tcp:14 of
msgid ""
"Commands come first and client addresses last; every address is written "
"as a Python address tuple, e.g. ``\"('127.0.0.1', 3000)\"``. There is no "
"limit on the number of commands or on the number of clients, and every "
"listed client receives the same command list. Two internal commands carry"
" the log back:"
msgstr ""

#: 9ef58aea395a436382e23f39797e3e8e PyFlow.command_control_extension_tcp:19 of
msgid "/command_log_chunk <chunk_file> <log_file>"
msgstr ""

#: 3361f3fb70584140989542af7c3361a7 PyFlow.command_control_extension_tcp:20 of
msgid ""
"sent by the client after it uploaded one log chunk through the file "
"transfer channel; the server appends the chunk's entries to that client's"
" log file"
msgstr ""

#: 2563d4e4d9744c2fb16d84690c2e94e2 PyFlow.command_control_extension_tcp:24 of
msgid ""
"sent by the client when the batch is over; the server merges every "
"collected log file into ``merged_logs.json``"
msgstr ""

#: PyFlow.command_control_extension_tcp:27 e40a302503cb4bdda5420aa79d0c57eb of
msgid ""
"A client captures the output of the running commands and uploads a chunk "
"every ``_LOG_CHUNK_BYTES`` of captured output (a smaller final chunk "
"closes each command), so a command that never stops is still tracked in "
"real time. Every chunk is appended to the same log file - "
"``logs_<ip>_<port>.json`` in the server's ``logs`` directory - which is "
"therefore never re-sent and never rewritten, only extended."
msgstr ""

#: 9209095513ec402980427a0ddd988219
#: PyFlow.command_control_extension_tcp.setup_server_commands:1 of
msgid "Register the control-extension commands on a server instance."
msgstr "在服务器实例上注册control-extension命令。"

#: 114b0a54c29747fd88bc2852eab174bf
#: PyFlow.command_control_extension_tcp.setup_client_commands:1 of
msgid "Register the control-extension commands on a client instance."
msgstr "在客户端实例上注册control-extension命令。"

